title: LSP Folding

Fold arrows appear on definitions, `<%if%>` clauses, multi-line widgets and elements, comments, code blocks and the `.tid` header, through `textDocument/foldingRange`. Try it in [[LSP Folding - (Example)]].

!! What folds

|! Construct |! Folds |
|`.tid` header |its fields, as a region |
|Multi-line definition |to the line before `\end`, which stays visible |
|`<%if%>` block |each clause on its own, up to the next clause or `<%endif%>` |
|Multi-line widget or element |to the line before its closing tag; an opening tag written over several lines also folds its content |
|Comment |the whole comment |
|Code block |to the line before its closing fence |

A tiddler that is not wikitext offers no folds.

!! Instead of indentation folding

Once a server offers folding, VS Code stops folding by indentation, so everything indentation used to fold has to fold here. Across `core/wiki/macros/toc.tid`, 109 of the 110 lines indentation folded still fold; the exception is text indented under a one-line comment.

A paragraph that ~TiddlyWiki wraps around several lines is no tag you wrote, so it does not fold. There is one fold per line, the widest, so the first clause of an `<%if%>` block folds as that clause, not as the whole block.